<title>USA: Smaller spec position limit urged for CSCE coffee. [CORRECTED 14:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Smaller spec position limit urged for CSCE coffee. [CORRECTED 14:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coffee, Sugar and Cocoa Exchange's coffee committee said it recommended the board of managers slash the speculative position limit on Coffee &quot;C&quot; futures from 500 to 200 lots during a contract's delivery period.</p>
<p>(Corrects that new postion limit applies only to contracts in notice period, not all accounts).</p>
<p>The recommendation is to be voted on by the board at its meeting today, CSCE said in a statement.</p>
<p>If the board approves the rule ammendment, it will then be submitted to Commodity Futures Trading Commission for approval. The rule would take effect beginning with the December 1996 contract.</p>
<p>--Wendy Pollack, New York Commodities Desk 212-859-1640</p>
